t people are finding there's some  sightings of spider-man and venom action  figures inside buildings and then like  electro referencing the ultimate  spider-man 2 game and Peter making jokes  referencing movies like Robocop and die  hard and oh [ __ ] did last summer but we  don't got time for all that let's move  on in the game you can also retrieve  several backpacks that are webbed up  around the city that contains various  spider-man collectables that are worth  mentioning let's run through what we  found one of them contains a business  card for Nelson and Murdock another a  vial of sand that spider-man thinks  could contain Sandman that he does one  unleash and then another a vial of the  lizard's blood then there's this  farewell card signed by Daily Bugle  staff including Eddie Brock who I'm sure  is very happy to see clearly there's  also a Spidey signal as well as a pin  for Spidey squad their YouTube channel  known for lots of coverage leading up to  the release of the game another item is  this drawing by a kid for whom  spider-man rescued a balloon which is a  nod to the lame side missions in the old  spider-man 2 game where if you had to  rescue balloons for kids it's gotta be  at least another item is a piece of the  helmet of Mysterio while another  contains a book called work-life balance  for idiots the author of that book is  dr. Ludwig Lionheart  actually one of the aliases of Mysterio  aka Quentin Beck another backpack  contains some spider-man suit arm  webbing that's the stuff from a very  early design of spider-man suit from the  60s and lastly another backpack in  Central Park there's a gaming device  that looks a lot like a PlayStation Vita  now another big source of fun details  comes from spider-man's social media  feed which you can access through the  map screen so let's run through some of  this cool stuff that we found one  account appears to be John Jameson Jay  jonah Jameson's son the astronaut I  spotted another account called got